    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1021">

                <pb facs="0771" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 412.00/36.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Minister, in chargé of American interests
                        in Mexico, to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="87" xml:id="d1021-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 54.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brazilian Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 7, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    translation of the decree issued by Venustiano Carranza, First Chief of the
                    Constitutionalist Army, under date of May 10, 1913, relative to the presentation
                    and settling of claims for damages and losses suffered by Mexicans and
                    foreigners since the beginning of the Civil War on the 21st day of November,
                    1910, to date.<anchor n="88" xml:id="d1021-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>It might be well to give this decree some publication in the American press so
                    that interested persons may be able to comply with the requirements of the
                    same.</p>
                <p>With assurances [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. M. Cardoso de
                    Oliveira</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d1021-a1.xml" xpointer="d1021-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1021-f1" n="87" type="source" xml:id="d1021-f1-content">
                <p>Receipt acknowledged Dec. 19, 1914.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1021-f2" n="88" xml:id="d1021-f2-content">
                <p>This decree is printed in <ref target="frus1913#pg_955">For. Rel. 1913, p.
                        955</ref>; but the text differs from the one here printed not only in
                    immaterial variations of translation hut also in two substantial particulars:
                    texts of Article V and Article VI.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
